{"id": "13a193f9-8553-41b4-a2db-2ecb1b5425b0", "slug": "global-agency-motion-opener-1", "title": "Global Agency - Motion Opener", "description": "Global Agency Footer Section is designed for organizing site-wide navigation, legal links, and utility content. Key features include multi-column navigation groups and clear legal pathways. It is suitable for SaaS websites, product marketing pages, and documentation hubs.", "content": "---\nversion: \"neuform-top-creators-featured\"\nname: \"Global Agency - Motion Opener\"\ndescription: \"Global Agency Footer Section is designed for organizing site-wide navigation, legal links, and utility content. Key features include multi-column navigation groups and clear legal pathways. It is suitable for SaaS websites, product marketing pages, and documentation hubs.\"\ncolors:\n  primary: \"#22C55E\"\n  secondary: \"#050505\"\n  accent: \"#22C55E\"\n  background: \"#050505\"\n  surface: \"#18181B\"\n  text-primary: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  text-secondary: \"#A1A1AA\"\n  border: \"#27272A\"\ntypography:\n  display-lg:\n    fontFamily: \"Inter\"\n    fontSize: \"64px\"\n    fontWeight: 500\n    lineHeight: \"1.04\"\n    letterSpacing: \"0\"\n  body-md:\n    fontFamily: \"Inter\"\n    fontSize: \"16px\"\n    fontWeight: 400\n    lineHeight: \"1.6\"\n  label-md:\n    fontFamily: \"JetBrains Mono\"\n    fontSize: \"12px\"\n    fontWeight: 600\n    lineHeight: \"1.2\"\nspacing:\n  base: \"8px\"\n  gap: \"16px\"\n  card-padding: \"24px\"\n  section-padding: \"80px\"\nrounded:\n  card: \"1px\"\n  control: \"8px\"\n  pill: \"9999px\"\ncomponents:\n  card:\n    background: \"Use the surface token with subtle borders and HTML-matched shadow depth\"\n    radius: \"Match the declared card radius token\"\n  button:\n    background: \"Use primary or accent colors for the main action\"\n    radius: \"Use the control or pill radius based on the source HTML\"\n---\n# Global Agency - Motion Opener\nSource: Neuform Featured templates from top creators. Author: Meng To (@mengto). Views: 245; favorites: 11; remixes: 3.\nTags: footer, animated, webgl, dither, effect, navigation, legal.\n## Overview\nGlobal Agency Footer Section is designed for organizing site-wide navigation, legal links, and utility content. Key features include multi-column navigation groups and clear legal pathways. It is suitable for SaaS websites, product marketing pages, and documentation hubs.\n\nTOKYO KYOTO Forged in Kyoto, scaling across global networks. Operating from our sanctuary in the historic district, we orchestrate global initiatives, extending our digital infrastructure through Asian hubs and worldwid…\n## Composition\nUse the attached HTML reference as the source of truth. Preserve the visible hierarchy, first-screen composition, section rhythm, density, and interaction tone before adapting copy or content.\nKey visible headings include: Forged in Kyoto, scaling across global networks..\n## Colors\nAnchor the palette in primary #22C55E, secondary #050505, accent #22C55E, background #050505, surface #18181B, text-primary #FFFFFF. Keep background, surface, text, and border roles distinct so generated layouts retain the same contrast pattern as the source.\n## Typography\nUse Inter for display moments and Inter for body copy unless the HTML clearly demands a compatible fallback. Labels and technical metadata should use JetBrains Mono or an equivalent mono face.\n## Layout\nKeep spacing deliberate and stable. Favor the same grid direction, max-width behavior, card density, and responsive stacking seen in the HTML. Do not replace distinctive source structures with generic SaaS sections.\n## Components\nCards, buttons, badges, navigation, and repeated blocks should preserve the source geometry, border treatment, and hover feel.\n## Motion\nPreserve existing motion cues such as masked reveals, staggered entrance, hover lift, scroll-triggered transitions, and ambient movement. Keep easing smooth and restrained.\n## WebGL & Effects\n\nIf the source includes canvas, WebGL, Three.js, gradients, particles, or atmospheric effects, rebuild them as supporting layers behind the content. Keep effects performant, responsive, and secondary to the interface.\n\n## Guardrails\n- Do not flatten the source into a generic card grid.\n- Do not swap the color mode unless the source clearly supports it.\n- Preserve the first viewport signal, focal object, and visual density.\n- Keep buttons, cards, and badges aligned to the same radius and border language.", "preview_html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Global Agency - Motion Opener</title>\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n    <link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n</head>\n<body class=\"antialiased h-screen w-screen overflow-hidden flex flex-col relative selection:bg-green-500/30 selection:text-green-200\" style=\"font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; background-color: #050505; color: #f5f5f5;\">\n\n    <!-- WebGL Laser Background -->\n    <canvas id=\"laser-canvas\" class=\"fixed top-0 left-0 w-full h-full pointer-events-none z-0\"></canvas>\n\n    <!-- CSS Halftone Layer -->\n    <div class=\"halftone-overlay\" style=\"position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; background-image: radial-gradient(circle, #22c55e 0.5px, transparent 0.5px); background-size: 6px 6px; opacity: 0.05; pointer-events: none; z-index: 0;\"></div>\n\n    <!-- Canvas Animated Halftone Dots Maps -->\n    <div class=\"absolute top-0 left-0 w-full h-[50vh] pointer-events-none z-10 hidden md:block\">\n        <div class=\"dot-map absolute top-12 left-[10%] w-[400px] h-[300px]\">\n            <canvas id=\"canvas-tk\" class=\"w-full h-full\"></canvas>\n            <div class=\"map-label absolute top-[60%] left-[55%] text-xs font-medium text-[#22c55e] tracking-widest translate-x-4 -translate-y-2\">TOKYO</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"dot-map absolute top-8 right-[5%] w-[500px] h-[350px]\">\n            <canvas id=\"canvas-ky\" class=\"w-full h-full\"></canvas>\n            <div class=\"map-label absolute top-[28%] left-[45%] text-xs font-medium text-[#22c55e] tracking-widest translate-x-4 -translate-y-2\">KYOTO</div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Main Content -->\n    <main class=\"flex-grow flex flex-col justify-end px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-16 pb-8 pt-[40vh] max-w-[1800px] mx-auto w-full z-20 relative\">\n\n        <!-- Headline -->\n        <h1 class=\"text-5xl md:text-7xl lg:text-8xl font-normal tracking-tighter leading-[1.05] max-w-[1200px]\" id=\"headline\">\n            Forged in\n            <span class=\"inline-block overflow-hidden align-middle mx-[0.2em] -translate-y-[0.1em]\">\n                <!-- Image Wrapper -->\n                <span class=\"img-reveal-inner block will-change-transform pr-0 p-[1px] bg-gradient-to-br from-green-400/50 via-green-800/20 to-green-300/40 rounded-sm shadow-xl\">\n                    <img src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1493976040374-85c8e12f0c0e?q=80&w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop\" alt=\"Kyoto Heritage Studio\" class=\"w-24 h-12 md:w-36 md:h-20 lg:w-48 lg:h-[6.5rem] object-cover rounded-[1px] block mix-blend-luminosity opacity-90\" />\n                </span>\n            </span>\n            Kyoto, <br class=\"hidden md:block\"/>scaling across global networks.\n        </h1>\n\n        <!-- Subheadline -->\n        <p class=\"mt-8 md:mt-10 text-lg md:text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-light tracking-tight text-neutral-400 leading-[1.3] max-w-[1000px]\" id=\"subhead\">\n            Operating from our sanctuary in the historic district, we orchestrate global initiatives, extending our digital infrastructure through Asian hubs and worldwide networks.\n        </p>\n\n    </main>\n\n    <!-- Footer -->\n    <footer class=\"px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-16 pb-8 pt-12 flex justify-between items-end w-full max-w-[1800px] mx-auto z-20 relative\">\n        <div class=\"foot-item text-[#22c55e] font-medium text-2xl tracking-tighter leading-none\" aria-label=\"Company Logo\">X</div>\n        <div class=\"foot-item text-xs md:text-xs font-normal tracking-widest text-neutral-500\">2030</div>\n    </footer>\n\n    <script>\n        gsap.registerPlugin();\n\n        // 1. Text Splitting Function for Orchestrated Reveal\n        function splitText(elementId, type = \"slide\") {\n            const el = document.getElementById(elementId);\n            if (!el) return;\n\n            const childNodes = Array.from(el.childNodes);\n            el.innerHTML = '';\n\n            childNodes.forEach(node => {\n                if (node.nodeType === 3) {\n                    const words = node.textContent.split(/\\s+/).filter(w => w.trim() !== '');\n                    words.forEach(word => {\n                        const wrapper = document.createElement('span');\n                        wrapper.style.display = 'inline-block';\n                        wrapper.style.verticalAlign = 'top';\n                        wrapper.style.marginRight = '-0.05em';\n\n                        if (type === \"slide\") {\n                            wrapper.style.overflow = 'hidden';\n                            wrapper.innerHTML = `<span class=\"reveal-inner\" style=\"display: inline-block; will-change: transform; padding-right: 0.25em; padding-bottom: 0.1em;\">${word}</span>`;\n                        } else {\n                            wrapper.style.overflow = 'visible';\n                            wrapper.innerHTML = `<span class=\"word-inner\" style=\"display: inline-block; will-change: transform; padding-right: 0.25em;\">${word}</span>`;\n                        }\n                        el.appendChild(wrapper);\n                    });\n                } else if (node.nodeType === 1) {\n                    el.appendChild(node);\n                }\n            });\n        }\n\n        // 2. Cinematic GSAP Master Timeline\n        window.addEventListener('load', () => {\n            splitText('headline', 'slide');\n            splitText('subhead', 'fade');\n\n            const prefersReducedMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;\n\n            if (prefersReducedMotion) {\n                gsap.from('main, footer, .dot-map, .halftone-overlay', { opacity: 0, duration: 1, stagger: 0.2 });\n                return;\n            }\n\n            const tl = gsap.timeline({ defaults: { ease: \"expo.out\" } });\n\n            // Base Scene State\n            gsap.set('#laser-canvas', { scale: 1.8, opacity: 0, filter: \"blur(30px)\" });\n            gsap.set('.halftone-overlay', { opacity: 0 });\n            gsap.set('.dot-map', { scale: 0.5, opacity: 0, filter: \"blur(20px)\" });\n            gsap.set('.map-label', { opacity: 0, letterSpacing: \"-0.2em\" });\n\n            gsap.set('#headline .reveal-inner', { y: '120%', skewY: 8, transformOrigin: \"0% 100%\" });\n            gsap.set('.img-reveal-inner', { scale: 0, filter: \"blur(15px)\", rotation: -15 });\n\n            gsap.set('#subhead .word-inner', { opacity: 0, scale: 1.5, filter: \"blur(12px)\", y: 20 });\n            gsap.set('footer .foot-item', { opacity: 0, y: 15 });\n\n            // SEQ 1: IGNITION\n            tl.to('#laser-canvas', { opacity: 1, scale: 1, filter: \"blur(0px)\", duration: 3.5, ease: \"power4.inOut\" })\n              .to('.halftone-overlay', { opacity: 0.05, duration: 2 }, \"-=1.5\");\n\n            // SEQ 2: NETWORK NODES\n            tl.to('.dot-map', { opacity: 1, scale: 1, filter: \"blur(0px)\", duration: 2.5, stagger: 0.15, ease: \"power4.out\" }, \"-=2.5\")\n              .to('.map-label', { opacity: 1, letterSpacing: \"0.1em\", duration: 1.2, stagger: 0.1, ease: \"power3.out\" }, \"-=2\")\n              .to('.map-label', { opacity: 0.4, duration: 0.05, yoyo: true, repeat: 5 }, \"-=1.5\");\n\n            // SEQ 3: THE BUILD (Headline Focus)\n            tl.to('#headline .reveal-inner', { y: '0%', skewY: 0, duration: 1.4, stagger: 0.03, ease: \"expo.out\" }, \"-=1.2\")\n              .to('.img-reveal-inner', { scale: 1, filter: \"blur(0px)\", rotation: 0, duration: 2, ease: \"elastic.out(1, 0.7)\" }, \"-=1.2\");\n\n            // SEQ 4: THE RESOLVE (Subhead & Interface)\n            tl.to('#subhead .word-inner', { opacity: 1, scale: 1, filter: \"blur(0px)\", y: 0, duration: 1.2, stagger: 0.01, ease: \"power3.out\" }, \"-=1.0\")\n              .to('footer .foot-item', { opacity: 1, y: 0, duration: 1.5, stagger: 0.1, ease: \"power2.out\" }, \"-=0.5\");\n\n            // Infinite Master Drift\n            gsap.to(['main', '.dot-map'], { scale: 1.02, duration: 20, ease: \"none\", delay: 1 });\n        });\n\n        // 3. WebGL Laser Background Component\n        function initLaser() {\n            const canvas = document.getElementById('laser-canvas');\n            const gl = canvas.getContext('webgl', { alpha: false, antialias: false });\n            if (!gl) return;\n\n            const vsSource = `\n                attribute vec2 position;\n                void main() {\n                    gl_Position = vec4(position, 0.0, 1.0);\n                }\n            `;\n\n            const fsSource = `\n                precision highp float;\n                uniform vec2 u_resolution;\n                uniform float u_time;\n\n                float hash(vec2 p) { return fract(sin(dot(p, vec2(12.9898, 78.233))) * 43758.5453); }\n                float noise(vec2 p) {\n                    vec2 i = floor(p); vec2 f = fract(p);\n                    f = f * f * (3.0 - 2.0 * f);\n                    return mix(mix(hash(i), hash(i + vec2(1.0, 0.0)), f.x),\n                               mix(hash(i + vec2(0.0, 1.0)), hash(i + vec2(1.0, 1.0)), f.x), f.y);\n                }\n                float fbm(vec2 p) {\n                    float v = 0.0; float a = 0.5;\n                    for(int i=0; i<4; i++) { v += a * noise(p); p *= 2.0; a *= 0.5; }\n                    return v;\n                }\n\n                void main() {\n                    vec2 uv = gl_FragCoord.xy / u_resolution.xy;\n                    float x = uv.x - 0.5;\n                    float y = uv.y;\n                    vec2 p = uv * vec2(u_resolution.x/u_resolution.y, 1.0);\n\n                    vec3 c_core = vec3(1.0, 1.0, 1.0);\n                    vec3 c_glow = vec3(0.13, 0.77, 0.36);\n                    vec3 c_smoke = vec3(0.03, 0.18, 0.08);\n                    vec3 c_particle = vec3(0.6, 0.95, 0.7);\n\n                    float bottomDist = 1.0 - y;\n                    float flare = smoothstep(0.8, 1.0, bottomDist);\n                    float spread = 1.0 + pow(flare, 4.0) * 4.0;\n                    float ax = x / spread;\n\n                    float core = exp(-abs(ax) * 4000.0);\n                    float innerGlow = exp(-abs(ax) * 600.0) * (1.0 + flare * 0.3);\n                    float outerGlow = exp(-abs(ax) * 150.0) * (0.4 + flare * 0.8);\n\n                    vec2 gridUv = uv * vec2(u_resolution.x/u_resolution.y * 700.0, 700.0);\n                    float dots = smoothstep(0.85, 1.0, sin(gridUv.x) * sin(gridUv.y));\n                    float particleMask = exp(-abs(ax) * 120.0);\n                    float particles = dots * particleMask * (0.4 + flare * 2.0);\n\n                    vec2 smokeUv = p * vec2(2.0, 1.0) - vec2(0.0, u_time * 0.12);\n                    smokeUv.x += fbm(p * 3.0 + u_time * 0.06) * 0.25;\n                    float n1 = fbm(smokeUv * 3.0);\n                    float wisps = pow(1.0 - abs(n1 * 2.0 - 1.0), 3.0);\n\n                    vec2 hairlineUv = p * vec2(4.0, 1.0) - vec2(0.0, u_time * 0.2);\n                    hairlineUv.x += fbm(p * 5.0 - u_time * 0.08) * 0.3;\n                    float n2 = fbm(hairlineUv * 6.0);\n                    float hairlines = pow(1.0 - abs(n2 * 2.0 - 1.0), 6.0);\n\n                    float smokeMask = exp(-abs(ax) * 45.0) * (0.8 + flare * 0.5);\n                    float smoke = (wisps * 0.8 + hairlines * 1.5) * smokeMask * 1.5;\n\n                    float pulse = 1.0 + 0.05 * sin(u_time * 4.0);\n\n                    vec3 color = vec3(0.02, 0.02, 0.02);\n                    color += core * c_core * 1.8;\n                    color += innerGlow * c_glow * pulse;\n                    color += outerGlow * c_glow * 0.5 * pulse;\n                    color += particles * c_particle * pulse;\n                    color += smoke * c_smoke;\n\n                    float ambientPool = exp(-abs(x) * 6.0) * pow(flare, 5.0) * 0.2;\n                    color += ambientPool * c_glow;\n\n                    vec2 rotCoord = vec2(\n                        (gl_FragCoord.x * 0.707 - gl_FragCoord.y * 0.707),\n                        (gl_FragCoord.x * 0.707 + gl_FragCoord.y * 0.707)\n                    );\n                    float ht = sin(rotCoord.x * 2.5) * sin(rotCoord.y * 2.5);\n\n                    float intensity = max(color.r, max(color.g, color.b));\n                    float halftoneMask = step(ht * 0.5 + 0.5, intensity * 2.5);\n\n                    float coreMask = smoothstep(0.4, 0.8, intensity);\n                    color = mix(color * (halftoneMask * 0.6 + 0.4), color, coreMask);\n\n                    gl_FragColor = vec4(color, 1.0);\n                }\n            `;\n\n            function createShader(gl, type, source) {\n                const shader = gl.createShader(type);\n                gl.shaderSource(shader, source);\n                gl.compileShader(shader);\n                return shader;\n            }\n\n            const program = gl.createProgram();\n            gl.attachShader(program, createShader(gl, gl.VERTEX_SHADER, vsSource));\n            gl.attachShader(program, createShader(gl, gl.FRAGMENT_SHADER, fsSource));\n            gl.linkProgram(program);\n            gl.useProgram(program);\n\n            const vertices = new Float32Array([-1, -1, 1, -1, -1, 1, 1, 1]);\n            const buffer = gl.createBuffer();\n            gl.bindBuffer(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, buffer);\n            gl.bufferData(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, vertices, gl.STATIC_DRAW);\n\n            const posLoc = gl.getAttribLocation(program, \"position\");\n            gl.enableVertexAttribArray(posLoc);\n            gl.vertexAttribPointer(posLoc, 2, gl.FLOAT, false, 0, 0);\n\n            const timeLoc = gl.getUniformLocation(program, \"u_time\");\n            const resLoc = gl.getUniformLocation(program, \"u_resolution\");\n\n            function resize() {\n                const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;\n                canvas.width = window.innerWidth * dpr;\n                canvas.height = window.innerHeight * dpr;\n                gl.viewport(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n                gl.uniform2f(resLoc, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n            }\n\n            window.addEventListener('resize', resize);\n            resize();\n\n            let startTime = performance.now();\n            function render() {\n                gl.uniform1f(timeLoc, (performance.now() - startTime) / 1000.0);\n                gl.drawArrays(gl.TRIANGLE_STRIP, 0, 4);\n                requestAnimationFrame(render);\n            }\n            render();\n        }\n        initLaser();\n\n        // 4. Canvas Animated Halftone Dot Maps Component\n        function initDotMap(canvasId, config) {\n            const canvas = document.getElementById(canvasId);\n            if (!canvas) return;\n            const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\n\n            let width, height;\n            const spacing = 6;\n            const radius = 0.5;\n            let time = 0;\n\n            function resize() {\n                const rect = canvas.parentElement.getBoundingClientRect();\n                const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;\n                width = rect.width;\n                height = rect.height;\n                canvas.width = width * dpr;\n                canvas.height = height * dpr;\n                ctx.scale(dpr, dpr);\n            }\n\n            window.addEventListener('resize', resize);\n            resize();\n\n            const cols = Math.floor(width / spacing);\n            const rows = Math.floor(height / spacing);\n\n            function render() {\n                ctx.clearRect(0, 0, width, height);\n\n                for (let i = 0; i < cols; i++) {\n                    for (let j = 0; j < rows; j++) {\n                        const x = i * spacing;\n                        const y = j * spacing;\n\n                        const nx = i / cols;\n                        const ny = j / rows;\n                        const density = config.shape(nx, ny);\n\n                        if (density > 0) {\n                            const isHighlight = Math.abs(i - config.hx) <= 2 && Math.abs(j - config.hy) <= 2;\n                            const isCenter = i === config.hx && j === config.hy;\n\n                            ctx.beginPath();\n                            ctx.arc(x, y, radius, 0, Math.PI * 2);\n\n                            if (isHighlight) {\n                                if (isCenter) {\n                                    ctx.fillStyle = '#22c55e';\n                                } else {\n                                    ctx.fillStyle = '#ffffff';\n                                }\n                            } else {\n                                const wave = Math.sin(time + nx * 10 + ny * 10) * 0.05;\n                                const alpha = Math.min(0.4, Math.max(0.05, density * 0.25 + wave));\n                                ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(34, 197, 94, ${alpha})`;\n                            }\n\n                            ctx.fill();\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n\n                time += 0.03;\n                requestAnimationFrame(render);\n            }\n\n            render();\n        }\n\n        initDotMap('canvas-tk', {\n            hx: 36,\n            hy: 29,\n            shape: (nx, ny) => {\n                const dx = nx - 0.4;\n                const dy = ny - 0.5;\n                const dist = Math.sqrt(dx*dx*1.5 + dy*dy);\n                return dist < 0.35 ? (1 - dist*2.5) : 0;\n            }\n        });\n\n        initDotMap('canvas-ky', {\n            hx: 38,\n            hy: 15,\n            shape: (nx, ny) => {\n                const dx = nx - 0.5;\n                const dy = ny - 0.5;\n                const dist = Math.sqrt(dx*dx + dy*dy*2.0);\n                return dist < 0.4 ? (1 - dist*2) : 0;\n            }\n        });\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>", "preview_file_name": "global-agency-motion-opener-1.html", "thumbnail_url": "https://hoirqrkdgbmvpwutwuwj.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/design-system-thumbnails/regenerated-2026-05-22-2s/global-agency-motion-opener-1.jpg", "source_name": "global-agency-motion-opener-1-DESIGN.md", "views": 472, "forks": 12, "private": false, "featured": true, "created_by": "9109ecbb-cdc4-4815-981e-2ea83be13765", "created_at": "2026-04-29T09:15:30.794547+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-07-03T21:10:41.108371+00:00"}